Tip Procedure: Write The Reporting Tracker



The tracker keeps the calendar columns emitted by the retained reports, in their legacy first-occurrence order (monthly archive order, then W3). No empty calendar periods are invented. A duplicate clinic/date would make legacy pivot_wider produce list cells that Feather cannot store. Fail with the multiplicity audit available; never silently resolve such cases.
s4a_diagnosis_tracker_fn &lt;- function(selection, path) {
  source &lt;- s4a_diagnosis_read_fn(selection)
  retained &lt;- paste0("SELECT *, 'y' || coalesce(CAST(CAST(cAnnee AS INTEGER) AS VARCHAR),'NA') || '_m' || coalesce(printf('%02d',CAST(cPeriode AS INTEGER)),'NA') report_date ",
    "FROM ", source, " WHERE selection IN ('expected','nearest_fallback')")
  duplicate &lt;- s4a_diagnosis_query_fn(paste0("SELECT count(*) n FROM (SELECT clinic_ID,report_date FROM (",
    retained, ") GROUP BY ALL HAVING count(*)&gt;1)")) |&gt; dplyr::collect()
  if (duplicate$n &gt; 0) stop("Legacy tracker has non-scalar clinic/date cells; inspect s4a_report_multiplicity_audit_df")
  dates &lt;- s4a_diagnosis_query_fn(paste0("SELECT report_date FROM (",
    retained, ") GROUP BY report_date ORDER BY min(report_order)")) |&gt; dplyr::collect()
  projection &lt;- vapply(dates$report_date, function(date) paste0(
    "coalesce(max(fname) FILTER (WHERE report_date=", s4a_diagnosis_literal_fn(date), "),0)::INTEGER AS ",
    s4a_diagnosis_identifier_fn(date)), character(1))
  s4a_diagnosis_write_fn(paste0("SELECT clinic_ID", if(length(projection)) paste0(",",paste(projection,collapse=",")),
    " FROM (", retained, ") GROUP BY clinic_ID ORDER BY min(report_order)"), path)
}
#| format: file
s4a_clinic_reporting_track_parquet &lt;- s4a_diagnosis_tracker_fn(
  s4a_clinic_reporting_selection_parquet,
  here::here("data/intermediates/clinic_reporting_track.parquet")
)








Tip Procedure: Write Retained And Legacy Rejected Diagnosis Groups



One branch per ordinary filename selector reads only its V columns. The two-path return is one file bundle per branch. Distinct selection keys prevent a join from multiplying measurements; original measurement rows, including W3 repeated keys with different values, remain intact. Both empty and nonempty rejected partitions have the same declared schema.
s4a_diagnosis_output_fn &lt;- function(group, dictionary, w12, w3, selection, directory) {
  vars &lt;- dictionary$var[!is.na(dictionary$filename) & dictionary$filename == group]
  stopifnot(length(group)==1L, grepl("^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$", group), length(vars)&gt;0)
  keys &lt;- c("clinic_ID","cAnnee","cPeriode","fname")
  projection &lt;- paste0("m.",s4a_diagnosis_identifier_fn(c(keys,vars)),collapse=",")
  joins &lt;- paste0("m.",keys," IS NOT DISTINCT FROM s.",keys,collapse=" AND ")
  sql &lt;- paste0("SELECT ", projection, " FROM ", s4a_diagnosis_read_fn(c(w12,w3)),
    " m JOIN (SELECT DISTINCT clinic_ID,cAnnee,cPeriode,fname,selection FROM ",
    s4a_diagnosis_read_fn(selection), ") s ON ", joins)
  retained &lt;- s4a_diagnosis_write_fn(paste0(sql," WHERE s.selection IN ('expected','nearest_fallback')"),
    file.path(directory,paste0(group,".parquet")))
  rejected &lt;- s4a_diagnosis_write_fn(paste0(sql," WHERE s.selection='wrong_fname'"),
    file.path(directory,paste0(group,"_wrong_fname.parquet")))
  c(retained=retained,wrong_fname=rejected)
}








